# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Commit template — rsc-web-picture-market
# Lines starting with # are stripped by git. Delete what does not apply.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# FORMAT:  <gitmoji> <type>(<scope>): <description>
#
#   type   : feat | fix | docs | test | refactor | perf | chore | build | ci
#   scope  : tools | labels | api | db-healthcheck | backend | frontend
#            | github | dev | config
#   gitmoji: ✨ feat  🐛 fix  📝 docs  🧪 test  ♻️ refactor  ⚡ perf  🔧 chore
#
# One line for the summary. Imperative mood, lowercase after the colon, no
# trailing period. Keep it under 72 characters.
#
# BODY — answer these three questions in order, one paragraph each:
#   What   : what changed, concretely. Name files and line numbers.
#   Against: which file, component or API this changes, and what it is
#            measured against.
#   Why   : the reason. The bug, the constraint, or the requirement that
#            makes this necessary — not a restatement of the diff.
#
# Rules that have bitten this repo before:
#   - Explain WHY, not WHAT the diff already shows. The diff is the what.
#   - If something surprising was found, say it and say how it was verified.
#   - If a check could not be run, say which and why. Do not imply coverage
#     you did not produce.
#
# FOOTER
#   Refs #<issue>   — reference the issue. Use "Refs", not "Fixes", unless
#                      the work genuinely closes it.
#   Refs #16        — issues in this repo are closed manually; the branch-pr
#                      process expects this exact form.
#
# NEVER add:
#   Co-Authored-By / Co-authored-by trailers
#   "Generated with Claude Code" or any AI attribution footer
#   AI/tooling name-dropping in the trailer block
#   The contributor is a human; authorship stays human.
#
# Example:
#   🐛 fix(tools): exit after printing help to stop an infinite loop
#
#   What: added a single `exit 0` at the end of usage().
#   Against: the -h|--help branch of the argument loop, which had no shift,
#   and usage(), which never returned. $# never decreased, so --help reprinted
#   usage forever: 1316 iterations, 42112 lines.
#   Why: printing help has to terminate the process anyway, so exit is correct
#   over shift. The code is 0 because help is a success; fail() owns exit 1.
#   Found by an assertion harness, not by reading the script -- manual
#   checking missed it because `--help | head -22` looked correct and SIGPIPE
#   hid the hang.
#
#   Refs #16